  "name": "Terasic Cyclone V GX Starter Kit (C5G)",
  "source": "Terasic Cyclone V GX Starter Kit User Manual (June 5, 2014; version 1.2.1 on the Terasic site; revision B hardware), tables 3-2 to 3-6. Compared pin by pin and I/O standard by I/O standard with two files of the C5G System CD v1.3.0: the golden top (Demonstrations/C5G_UART_USB_LED/C5G_golden_top.qsf), where HEX2 and HEX3 are GPIO[22] to GPIO[35], and the factory demo (Demonstrations/C5G_Default/C5G_Default.qsf): 65 of 65 equal. The FPGA is alone in the JTAG chain with JP2 shorted (pins 1-2), and the CD programs it at @1.",
